(One of the roots that govern two accusatives, see examples below)
.²1 To carry, lead, bring, convey, take, conduct; {#ajAM grAmaM nayati#}
 <ls>Sk.</ls>; {#naya mAM navena vasatiM payomucA#} <ls>V. 4. 43</ls>.
.²2 To guide, direct, govern; {#mUQaH parapratyayaneyabudDiH#} <ls>M. 1. 2</ls>.
.²3 To lead away to, carry or bring away; {#sItA laNkAM nItA surAriRA#}
 <ls>Bk. 6. 49</ls>; <ls>R. 12. 103</ls>; <ls>Ms. 6. 88</ls>.
.²4 To carry off; <ls>Śānti. 3. 5</ls>.
.²5 To carry off for oneself (<ab>Ātm.</ab>).
.²6 To spend, or pass (as time); {#yenAmandamarande daladaravinde dinAnyanAyizata#}
 <ls>Bv. 1. 10</ls>; {#nItvA mAsAn katicit#} <ls>Me. 2</ls>; {#saMvizwaH kuSaSayane niSAM#}
 {#ninAya#} <ls>R. 1. 95</ls>.
.²7 To bring or reduce any person to any state or condition; {#tamapi taralatAmanayadanaNgaH#}
 <ls>K. 143</ls>; {#nItastvayA paYcatAm#} <ls>Ratn. 3. 3</ls>; <ls>R. 8. 19</ls>. (In this sense the
 root is used with substantives much in the same way as {#kf#} <ab>q. v.</ab>);
 {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} {#duHKaM nI#} to reduce to misery; {#vaSaM nI#} to reduce to
 subjection, win over; {#astaM nI#} to cause to set; {#vinASaM nI#} to destroy;
 {#paritozaM nI#} to gratify, please; {#SUdratAM-dAsatvaM#} <ab>&c.</ab> {#nI#}
 to reduce to the state of a Śūdra, slave <ab>&c.</ab>; {#sAkzyaM nI#} to admit
 as a witness; {#daRqaM nI#} to inflict punishment upon, to punish; {#punaruktatAM#}
 {#nI#} to render superfluous; {#vikrayaM nI#} to sell; {#BasmatAM-BasmasAt#}
 {#nI#} to reduce to ashes <ab>&c.</ab>
.²8 To ascertain, investigate, inquire into, settle, decide; {#CalaM nirasya#}
 {#BUtena vyavahArAnnayennfpaH#} <ls>Y. 2. 19</ls>; {#evaM SAstrezu Binnezu bahuDA#}
 {#nIyate kriyA#} <ls>Mb.</ls>
.²9 To trace, track, find out; {#etErliNgErnayet sImAm#} <ls>Ms. 8. 252</ls>, <ls n="Ms. 8.">256</ls>;
 {#yaTA nayatyasfkpAtErmfgasya mfgayuH padam#} <ls n="Ms.">8. 44</ls>; <ls>Y. 2. 151</ls>.
.²10 To marry.
.²11 To exclude from.
.²12 (<ab>Ātm.</ab>) To instruct, give instruction in; {#SAstre nayate#} <ls>Sk.</ls>
